  "properties": {
    "video_key": "pl-teaching-moves-paradigm-shift",
    "instructions_important": "false",
    "skip_dialog": true,
    "skip_sound": true,
    "parent_level_id": 28811,
    "name_suffix": "_2026",
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "\r\n\r\nThis unit represents a fundamental change in computer science learning. Students move from writing code line by line to directing, evaluating, and refining what AI produces.\r\n\r\n## Misconceptions \r\n\r\nThis shift can feel uncomfortable at first. It challenges what we expect learning and teaching to look like. These common misconceptions reflect that tension.\r\n\r\nClick on each one to see how it reframes into a new way of thinking.\r\n\r\n<div style=\"max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">\r\n  <div style=\"display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 16px; justify-content: space-between;\">\r\n\r\n<!-- Card 1 -->\r\n<div style=\"flex: 1 1 calc(50% - 16px); min-width: 300px; box-sizing: border-box;\">\r\n<details style=\"border: 2px solid #0093a4; border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden; background-color: #ffffff;\">\r\n        <summary style=\"background-color: #0093a4; color: #ffffff; padding: 18px; cursor: pointer; font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold; list-style: none;\">\r\n          “Students aren’t learning if they don’t write the code.”\r\n        </summary>\r\n        <div style=\"padding: 18px; background-color: #ffffff; border-top: 2px solid #0093a4;\">\r\n          <div style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #4a4a4a; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; margin-bottom: 10px;\">\r\n            Shift in Understanding\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 12px; line-height: 1.5;\">\r\n            Students focus on reasoning, not just syntax.<br>\r\n            Ask: “What does this code do?” and “Why does it work?”\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #333333; background-color: #b2dee3; padding: 12px; border-radius: 6px; line-height: 1.5;\">\r\n            Understanding hasn’t disappeared. It’s moved. Students show learning by explaining, evaluating, and improving code, not just writing it.\r\n          </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </details>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n<!-- Card 2 -->\r\n<div style=\"flex: 1 1 calc(50% - 16px); min-width: 300px; box-sizing: border-box;\">\r\n      <details style=\"border: 2px solid #0093a4; border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden; background-color: #ffffff;\">\r\n        <summary style=\"background-color: #0093a4; color: #ffffff; padding: 18px; cursor: pointer; font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold; list-style: none;\">\r\n          “I need to know all the code to teach this.”\r\n        </summary>\r\n        <div style=\"padding: 18px; background-color: #ffffff; border-top: 2px solid #0093a4;\">\r\n          <div style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #4a4a4a; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; margin-bottom: 10px;\">\r\n            Shift in the Teacher’s Role\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 12px; line-height: 1.5;\">\r\n            Coach thinking instead of providing answers.<br>\r\n            Ask: “What did you try?” and “What could you change?”\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #333333; background-color: #b2dee3; padding: 12px; border-radius: 6px; line-height: 1.5;\">\r\n            You do not need to know every line of code. Your role is to guide how students think, question, and iterate.\r\n          </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </details>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n<!-- Card 3 -->\r\n<div style=\"flex: 1 1 calc(50% - 16px); min-width: 300px; box-sizing: border-box;\">\r\n      <details style=\"border: 2px solid #0093a4; border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden; background-color: #ffffff;\">\r\n        <summary style=\"background-color: #0093a4; color: #ffffff; padding: 18px; cursor: pointer; font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold; list-style: none;\">\r\n          “How do I know what the student did vs. AI?”\r\n        </summary>\r\n        <div style=\"padding: 18px; background-color: #ffffff; border-top: 2px solid #0093a4;\">\r\n          <div style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #4a4a4a; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; margin-bottom: 10px;\">\r\n            Shift in Evaluation\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 12px; line-height: 1.5;\">\r\n            Look for evidence of process: prompts, iterations, and revisions.<br>\r\n            Require explanation and reflection.\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #333333; background-color: #b2dee3; padding: 12px; border-radius: 6px; line-height: 1.5;\">\r\n            Learning is visible in how students direct, test, and improve, not just in what they submit.\r\n          </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </details>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n<!-- Card 4 -->\r\n<div style=\"flex: 1 1 calc(50% - 16px); min-width: 300px; box-sizing: border-box;\">\r\n      <details style=\"border: 2px solid #0093a4; border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden; background-color: #ffffff;\">\r\n        <summary style=\"background-color: #0093a4; color: #ffffff; padding: 16px 18px; cursor: pointer; font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold; list-style: none; min-height: 40px; display: flex; align-items: center;\">\r\n  “If it works, they’re done.”\r\n</summary>\r\n        <div style=\"padding: 18px; background-color: #ffffff; border-top: 2px solid #0093a4;\">\r\n          <div style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #4a4a4a; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; margin-bottom: 10px;\">\r\n            Shift in the Locus of Skill\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 12px; line-height: 1.5;\">\r\n            Emphasize directing, refining, and extending solutions.<br>\r\n            Ask: “How can you improve it?” and “Can you adapt it?”\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: #333333; background-color: #b2dee3; padding: 12px; border-radius: 6px; line-height: 1.5;\">\r\n            A working product is the starting point, not the endpoint. The real skill is making decisions and iterating toward better solutions.\r\n          </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </details>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br><br>"
  },
